@startuml
left to right direction

actor Student
actor Administrator

rectangle "Smart Campus Study Room Booking System" {
  usecase "Book Room" as UC1
  usecase "View Room Availability" as UC2
  usecase "Cancel Own Booking" as UC3
  usecase "Block Room" as UC4
  usecase "Unblock Room" as UC5
  usecase "Review Room Usage" as UC6
  usecase "Send Booking Confirmation" as UC7
}

Student --> UC1
Student --> UC2
Student --> UC3

Administrator --> UC4
Administrator --> UC5
Administrator --> UC6

' why: R4 - every successful booking produces a confirmation
UC1 ..> UC7 : <<include>>

note right of UC1
R1: Booking starts in the future,
duration > 0 and <= 2 hours.
R2: Active bookings for the same
room cannot overlap.
R3: A blocked room cannot accept
a new booking.
end note

note right of UC7
R4: A successful booking
produces a confirmation.
end note

note bottom of UC3
A student can cancel only
their own bookings.
end note

note bottom of UC4
Blocking prevents new bookings.
The scenario does not specify
what happens to existing bookings.
end note

note bottom of UC1
Assumption: bookings whose time
boundaries only touch do not overlap.
end note

@enduml